## Instructions for Claude

You are working on the **{{ .ProjectPrefix }}** project managed by mtix. Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for the full operating guide.

## First-Time Setup

If skill files are not yet installed, run:
```
mtix plugin install --target claude-code
```
This installs 5 skill files and 4 compliance reference checklists to `.claude/skills/`.

## MCP Tools

mtix exposes tools via MCP (Model Context Protocol). Use the `mcp__mtix__` prefixed tools when available — they are preferred over CLI commands:

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `mcp__mtix__mtix_context` | **MANDATORY** — assemble full context chain before any work |
| `mcp__mtix__mtix_ready` | Find available work |
| `mcp__mtix__mtix_claim` | Claim a node |
| `mcp__mtix__mtix_done` | Mark work complete |
| `mcp__mtix__mtix_show` | View node details |
| `mcp__mtix__mtix_create` | Create a new node |
| `mcp__mtix__mtix_decompose` | Batch create children |
| `mcp__mtix__mtix_update` | Update node fields |
| `mcp__mtix__mtix_search` | Full-text search |
| `mcp__mtix__mtix_briefing` | **List nodes in briefing format** — labeled text blocks for context. Use instead of writing stub code to parse mtix_list output. Accepts multi-value filters (`under`, `status`, `type`, `fields`). |
| `mcp__mtix__mtix_comment` | Add traceability comment |
| `mcp__mtix__mtix_session_start` | Start work session |
| `mcp__mtix__mtix_session_end` | End work session |
| `mcp__mtix__mtix_agent_heartbeat` | Send heartbeat (every 5 min) |

## Key Rules

1. **Always call `mcp__mtix__mtix_context` before doing any work** — the assembled prompt is your complete briefing
2. Start a session before doing work, end it when done
3. Claim nodes before working on them
4. Follow the state machine — no shortcuts
5. Send heartbeats every 5 minutes to avoid stale detection
6. **Never leave tasks empty** — after `create` or `decompose`, every task MUST have `description`, `prompt`, and `acceptance` populated
7. Add a traceability comment before marking done: task → requirement → test → result
8. No stub implementations — functions must perform their documented purpose end-to-end
9. **Run `mtix sync` before you commit or push `.mtix/tasks.json`** — MCP tool results do not show the auto-import notices, so a write can succeed while the board on disk is a pulled one mtix has not imported. Commit it only when `Last auto-import refusal` does not read `pending`; otherwise follow the "Auto-import of .mtix/tasks.json Refused" procedure in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md)

## Best Practices for Claude

- **Prefer MCP tools over CLI** when both are available — MCP tools return structured data
- **Batch operations** — use `mcp__mtix__mtix_decompose` instead of multiple `mcp__mtix__mtix_create` calls
- **Search before creating** — use `mcp__mtix__mtix_search` to check for existing similar tasks
- **Use briefing format for analysis** — call `mcp__mtix__mtix_briefing` with multi-value filters instead of writing Python/jq post-processing code. Example: `mtix_briefing(under="PROJ-1,PROJ-2", status="done", type="issue", fields="id,title,prompt")`
- **Progress checks** — use `mcp__mtix__mtix_progress` to verify rollup before reporting completion

## Error Handling

If you encounter an error, check [TROUBLESHOOTING.md](TROUBLESHOOTING.md) for common solutions. If a command prints `mtix: auto-import of .mtix/tasks.json refused`, nothing was imported: never run the `--mode replace` import it names just to silence it, because that deletes the comments, activity and tasks it lists; follow the "Auto-import of .mtix/tasks.json Refused" procedure in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md). If blocked, record the reason with `mtix_comment`, then call `mtix_defer` (with an optional `until` wake time) rather than abandoning the task. Always document anomalies with `mtix_comment`.

If `mtix sync doctor` fails its `quarantined events` check, `mtix sync pull` has held pulled events it could not validate or apply; every pull retries them. Run `mtix sync pull` again; if events remain, list them with `mtix sync quarantine list` (read-only) and give the operator the event ids and reasons. **Never** delete quarantine rows, edit the local database, or raise `sync.max_lamport_jump` without a human's confirmation.

`mtix sync clone` refuses, naming the event and writing nothing, while the hub holds an event that fails these checks: recover with `mtix sync reconcile --discard-local --yes`, then `mtix sync pull` (which quarantines it), never any other way.
